"""Report narrative and proposed migration contracts; no source application code."""

OPENING = [
('What went wrong', [
('Finding', 'The current Builder ERP is not a full functional replacement for JAKH ERP. The earlier study described broad scope and a simpler navigation, but implementation started before a complete function, business-rule, data and exception mapping. That was an execution error. The user should not have had to identify the missing functions.'),
('What is real today', 'The original local application implements purchase-request drafting, repricing, submission, return and independent approval; scoped reads/search; request history; and a deterministic cost report from synthetic opening snapshots. Other screens mainly display synthetic records. These are useful foundations, but they do not reproduce most source workflows.'),
('What is materially missing', 'Estimate pricing and award handover; project/location/WBS setup; budget release and revisions; procurement through receipts and bills; measured client and subcontract certificates; stock and cost ledgers; finance and reconciliation; programme interfaces; controlled document/NCR/closeout workflows; people operations; administrative builders and integrations.'),
('Correction', 'Treat business capability preservation as a prerequisite for each implementation increment. Keep the selected Project briefing visual direction, but replace shallow categories and generic data with typed records, explicit rules, linked transactions and traceable acceptance evidence. No existing function is silently removed because its navigation is busy.'),
('What this package delivers', 'A comparison of all 42 recorded primary areas and all 267 recorded destination controls, 21 detailed workstream comparisons, a specific requirement and acceptance example for each destination, source-evidence references, proposed data contracts and a correction sequence. The companion searchable register and CSV carry all 267 rows.'),
('What it does not claim', 'No full migration, production readiness or rule parity is certified. Read-only UI evidence cannot prove hidden validation, permissions, every exception or a complete source data dictionary. Those remaining verification items are explicitly recorded, not treated as completed features.')]),
('Evidence and status rules', [
('Source baseline', 'The earlier Revision 4 study is 53 pages. Its archive contains the expanded administrator navigation (41-admin-navigation-expanded-ax.txt) and numbered screen/form evidence. Parsing that navigation yields 363 buttons: 96 groups and 267 leaves across 42 primary areas. Leaves are destination controls, not necessarily 267 unique business functions.'),
('Fresh verification', 'On 28 October 2026 the live dashboard was reopened in both My Company and JAKH Demo Contracting LLC contexts. The same 42 primary areas were visible. The Marina Gate project control report was opened and its basis captured again. This verifies those screens now; it is not a fresh walkthrough of all 267 destinations. Opening the source report generated a report-view record; no business transaction was edited, approved, posted, paid, closed or deleted.'),
('Source confidence', 'Every register row has menu evidence. Only rows with direct saved form/report evidence receive a stronger observation label; linked records and domain-level observations are distinguished. A visible instruction is a stated rule, not proof that all service paths enforce it. Empty filtered/sample lists are never proof of absence.'),
('Builder baseline', 'Compared application commit 3d941a0. Inspected schema and service/routes in app/server/db.mjs, http.mjs and service.mjs, plus the UI catalogue and examples. The 30 previously passing tests cover the current limited implementation. They are not 30 migration tests. No application code changed during this correction review.'),
('Register statuses', 'Partial implementation means a relevant executable subset exists, with the gap stated. Example only means read-only synthetic content, without the required workflow. Not implemented means no corresponding operational service. No row is certified as full parity. Each acceptance example is proposed and NOT RUN for migration parity.'),
('Read the evidence correctly', 'The sample-pack upgrade called a migration in earlier implementation notes only adds synthetic examples to the local database. It is not a JAKH export/import. Likewise, 24 guide destinations and 102 examples say nothing about complete coverage of 267 source controls. Source records, filenames and hashes are indexed in the evidence manifest.')]),
('A concrete piece of JAKH logic to preserve', [
('Fresh source example', 'The Marina Gate control report opened during this review shows revised budget AED 26,650,000; actual cost AED 14,055,081.01; forecast final cost AED 26,117,000; commitments AED 7,231,498; forecast margin AED 6,702,835; and matched posted receipts AED 15,675,795.22. These are demo-source observations, not migrated Builder balances.'),
('Meaning, not just numbers', 'The report calls AED 533,000 below budget forecast headroom, not realised profit. Four of four WBS have approved forecasts. Its stated fallback for a WBS without an approved forecast is revised budget, clearly provisional. The Builder report currently reads synthetic final totals and has no approved-forecast selection or fallback history.'),
('Progress has three meanings', 'Physical progress is 64.80%; certified financial progress 65.14%; posted billing progress 55.28%. The source explains original-budget weighting, certified gross and posted billing gross. These must not be collapsed into one generic project-completion percentage.'),
('Scope and allocation are explicit', 'Whole-project performance remains for the whole project; WBS, BOQ, location and discipline filters affect the detail table. Four unallocated detail rows remain visible. The new UI must label these two populations clearly, or explicitly change the behaviour; a filtered detail total must never be presented as if it explained an unchanged whole-project summary.'),
('Cost and cash are not interchangeable', 'The calculation basis says received exposure is not added to actual costs, WBS forecasts are not silently split by building, and matched receipts are tax-inclusive posted allocations including advances/retention. Credits/write-offs are excluded and bank clearance is not asserted. These are specific source rules requiring original services and reconciliation.'),
('Required implementation proof', 'Reproduce this type of report from migrated transactional facts and approved versions, then reconcile each measure and drill-down at the same cutoff. Test missing forecast, unallocated location, credit/correction, partial receipt and bank clearing. Copying displayed totals into new sample cards does not establish equivalence.')]),
('Keep the simple interface; restore the depth', [
('Stable starting points', 'My Work, Tenders, Projects and Company remain the four main routes. A selected project retains Overview, Plan, Site, Buying, Costs & Contracts, Documents and Handover. These are stable browse destinations, not a limit on business capability.'),
('Make missing functions findable', 'Plan needs Work & budget, Programme, Look-ahead and Constraints. Buying needs Requests, Sourcing, Orders & deliveries and Subcontracts. Costs & Contracts needs Client contract, Claims & certificates, Cost control/forecasts, Changes, Advances/retention, Securities and Final account. Documents needs Drawings, Submittals, Specifications/methods/ITPs, RFIs, Correspondence and Reviews. Company needs explicit Finance, People, Assets & fleet, Stores, Contacts & catalogue, Reports and Administration.'),
('One record, several useful views', 'A subcontract package is canonical. Site staff open measurements, commercial staff open certificates, finance opens bills/payments and managers see the package balance. Each view links the same source chain. The user does not re-enter project, company, scope or quantities at every stage.'),
('Simple record anatomy', 'Start with identity/location, status, current owner, next action, due date and blockers. Then show a clear work table and totals. Evidence, commercial terms, related records and history open on demand. Tabs are retained when they represent meaningful distinct work, not repeated blindly in each next screen.'),
('Findability and context', 'Provide purpose-labelled directories, global and scoped search, saved filters, familiar legacy synonyms and direct source links. Return restores filters and scroll. Every action shows legal company and currency. Explain empty, restricted, missing and stale data separately. A role changes priorities and authority, not the meaning of a label.'),
('Validation still required', 'The user selected a visual direction, not every proposed label. Test bid pricing, a partial delivery, a returned certificate, a location NCR, a disputed change and final settlement with representative roles. Record first destination, unassisted completion, wrong turns, time and missing information. No claim of the best possible usability or completed user validation is made.')]),
]

ADDITIONS = [
('Multiple companies and currencies', [
('Observed versus required', 'JAKH visibly separates companies/currencies and shows company-currency construction contracts/requisitions. Builder has service-level company/project scope for its current records and sample AED/USD companies. Neither the screenshots nor a company selector prove the full legal-entity accounting, consolidation or intercompany controls requested.'),
('Company foundation', 'A legal entity owns its functional currency, fiscal periods, taxes/localisation, journals/numbering, bank instructions and authority policy. Shared projects or joint ventures require entity-owned obligations and explicit allocations. Group reporting must distinguish management aggregation from financial consolidation and eliminations.'),
('Purchase request to order', 'An early unsourced demand can use a provisional company-currency estimate. On vendor selection use a valid product-specific quote, then an applicable agreement, then that vendor/company permitted preference. Show transaction currency and company equivalent, rate direction/source/date and provisional status. Never infer currency only from country or relabel an old amount when vendor changes.'),
('Changes and settlement', 'Changing vendor, quote, currency, quantity, tax or freight recalculates landed value and authority/budget checks; material changes route for reapproval. One order has one legal buyer, vendor and transaction currency. Recognition and settlement retain their own rates; authorised finance handles realised/unrealised FX, precision and lock periods.'),
('Concrete fixture', 'Company A (AED) requests 100 units quoted at USD 10. With a frozen example rate 3.67 AED/USD, amount is USD 1,000 / AED 3,670. Switching to an EUR 9 quote at example rate 4.00 gives EUR 900 / AED 3,600, with changed terms and a new review basis. These are synthetic test rates, not current market rates.'),
('Required proof', 'Reject cross-company references, missing/stale rates and unauthorised rate overrides in services, exports and AI. Test currencies with different minor units, split orders, partial receipt/payment, credit, intercompany transactions and historical reporting. Current money formatting assumes two minor digits and cannot yet claim general multi-currency accounting.')]),
('Every report begins with findings', [
('The report contract', 'Every report, including custom reports, must declare company/project/population, period/cutoff, currency and tax basis, included states, permissions, data freshness, definition/rule version and snapshot ID. Summary and rows use the same full authorised result, never just the displayed page.'),
('Calculation path', 'Authorised source facts -> validated allocations/state/cutoff -> metrics and reconciliation -> ranked deterministic findings -> rendered report/export. Optional AI may explain those findings using their evidence links. It must not calculate unverified totals, invent a cause or change the population.'),
('Finding structure', 'Each finding has type/severity, exact metric/value/unit, comparison basis, affected record IDs, evidence links, known limitation, owner and suggested next action where meaningful. Facts, estimates, assumptions and suggestions remain visibly different.'),
('Example findings', 'Cost: forecast exceeds revised budget because of named quantified variances; show missing forecast coverage. Procurement: five overdue lines, with remaining quantities and delivery dates. NCR: three cases awaiting verification, oldest 14 days, with responsible parties. Cash: expected shortfall in week 4 based on stated receipt/payment assumptions, separate from posted bank balance.'),
('Current gap', 'Builder implements only the illustrative cost-position report. It has no period-selectable transactional report engine or report families for ledger, aging, cash, certificates, stock, resources, quality or documents. JAKH already has a richer control-report basis, including explicit provisional forecast fallback and unallocated facts, which the new design must preserve or consciously change.'),
('Acceptance', 'Change filter/cutoff/permissions/currency and require matching summary, totals and export; test empty versus missing, credits/reversals, pagination, duplicate sources and unallocated amounts. Every number must reconcile to rows and original transactions. Unsupported AI claims trigger deterministic fallback.')]),
('Strategic AI without weakening control', [
('Priority 1: trusted retrieval and explanations', 'Put evidence-backed search beside the current task. Find the current permitted drawing revision, explain a cost variance from report findings, summarise an approval history or locate the contractual source of an obligation. Measure citation validity and factual support before launch.'),
('Priority 2: reviewable capture and drafts', 'Tender: extract BOQ/obligations with page/row citations. Buying: extract quote lines and flag differences in units, exclusions and delivery. Site: draft diary entries from notes/photos. NCR: organise evidence and suggest missing information; QA chooses cause and remedy. Documents: draft an RFI from the current drawing. Every extracted value remains reviewable before becoming a business record.'),
('Priority 3: connected review assistance', 'Subcontracts: assemble claimed versus accepted quantities and missing attachments. Changes/delay: build a cited event timeline and draft an assessment. Handover: check expected deliverables by location/system. Finance: suggest matches and explain exceptions from deterministic facts. A document checklist is not technical acceptance; a suggested match is not a posted settlement.'),
('Later: prediction only with evidence', 'Maintenance predictions, waste trends, schedule risk and cash scenarios need representative history, calibrated uncertainty and measured benefit. Generic chat across the ERP is not a substitute for governed data or a working transaction system.'),
('Control boundary', 'Use the requesting user/company/project permissions for retrieval, tools, files, caches and exports. Uploaded content is untrusted. AI cannot silently approve, post, pay, release retention, close a contract, change bank details or make external commitments. External provider/region/retention policy and secret management remain configuration gates.'),
('Acceptance and current state', 'Evaluate hallucinated citations, wrong revision, cross-company leakage, malicious documents, stale facts, unsupported numerical claims, correction effort, latency/cost and outage fallback. Builder currently has deterministic Explain findings only; no model integration or AI-backed workflow is implemented.')]),
('Construction gaps beyond the old menus', [
('Do not confuse preservation with sufficiency', 'The user requested a rich construction ERP from bid to handover. Preserve observed JAKH strengths and add missing lifecycle controls where needed. The following are explicit required capabilities or proposed details, not claims that the legacy software already enforces them.'),
('NCR, waste and safety', 'Full containment/cause/disposition/verification/reopen; quality hold points; HSE-specific authority/privacy; measured material loss, reuse and disposal evidence; linked rework cost/time. A general issue card or stock-scrap button alone is insufficient.'),
('Change and delay', 'One change event links instructions, contractual notices/deadlines, scope/rate/quantity assessment, owner and subcontract impacts, time impact, approvals/dispute and the resulting budget/order/programme versions. Keep proposed, instructed, priced, approved and certified effects distinct.'),
('Handover and defects', 'Readiness by building/floor/unit/system; inspections/tests/commissioning; as-builts; O&M; training; installed assets/warranties; partial acceptance; snags and reopening; defect-liability dates; final certificates and authorised releases. Technical completion, client acceptance and financial settlement are different states.'),
('Asset and people depth', 'Owned/hired contractor plant needs custody, transfer, availability, utilisation and cost. Installed assets need client handover evidence. HR menus require functional inspection; payroll, recruitment depth and statutory localisation are explicit open scope checks, never silently assumed complete or excluded.'),
('Design implication', 'Each case has one home and clear related work. A missing feature should appear in the implementation register with owner, data, rules and acceptance evidence, not be represented as a completed sample card.')]),
('Original data architecture required', [
('What must change', 'The existing records table stores most non-request examples as details JSON, with arbitrary strings for location and owner. This is appropriate for a demonstration but cannot enforce stock quantities, cumulative measurements, versioned terms, finance balances or cross-record authority.'),
('Shared backbone', 'Use typed entities for company, project, party and company terms, product/UOM, WBS, hierarchical location/system, currency/rate snapshot, document/revision, user/role, policy version and audit event. Keep stable IDs, source legacy IDs, effective dates and archived state. Descriptive JSON may supplement typed data, never replace business invariants.'),
('Transaction families', 'Estimate/assembly/BOQ/version; contract/BOQ revision; budget/revision/reservation; requisition/RFQ/quote/order lines; stock movements; subcontract application/service/certificate; client certificate; invoice/journal/payment/reconciliation; forecast/schedule snapshots; NCR/documents/diaries; time/asset/handover records.'),
('Consistency', 'State transitions happen in services with permission, validation, atomic persistence and version checks. Posting/acceptance uses unique source keys so retries do not duplicate facts. Immutable approved/posting snapshots have explicit reversal/correction links. Business audit covers all domains, not just requests.'),
('Location and cost grain', 'Store both work structure and physical structure; a WBS is not a floor and a BOQ line is not an account. Fact allocations explicitly connect work item, resource, location, period and company. Missing allocation remains visible and reconcilable. Never split WBS totals among buildings without an approved basis.'),
('Scope of the mapping file', 'The supplied data-contract CSV maps visible source field labels/concepts to proposed original target entities and identifies present gaps. It is not an extraction schema or executable importer. Exact source identifiers, column types, relations, attachments and full record counts still need a legitimate source export/data dictionary.')]),
('Migration sequence and reconciliation', [
('1. Obtain a controlled source snapshot', 'Use a read-only export or backup supplied through an authorised source process. Inventory entities, records, custom fields, attachments, integration definitions, permissions and histories. Record extraction cutoff, source version and checksums. Demo resets nightly and cannot serve as the production migration baseline. No source code is imported.'),
('2. Stage and map without losing evidence', 'Keep source payloads immutable in a restricted staging area. Map stable legacy IDs to new IDs; normalise company, currencies, UOM, parties, work/location structures and status meanings. Quarantine unresolved links/duplicates/missing values with reasons. Do not fabricate zeros, approvals or historical actors.'),
('3. Import dependency order', 'Companies/reference data -> identity/permissions -> parties/products -> projects/locations/WBS -> approved tender/contract/budget versions -> operational documents and stock/assets/time -> financial open items/ledger according to agreed history policy -> attachments/audit -> reporting facts and integration checkpoints. Preserve original timestamps and link every migrated row to the batch.'),
('4. Reconcile before accepting', 'Compare counts by entity/company/status, stable IDs, referential integrity, amounts by currency, quantities/UOM and attachment hashes. Reconcile original/revised BOQ/budgets, open commitments, stock quantity/valuation, certified quantities, retention/advances, AP/AR, trial balance, bank balances and forecast versions. Document every exclusion/adjustment and require zero unexplained differences.'),
('5. Rehearse and recover', 'Run imports repeatedly in disposable local copies; prove idempotency and interrupted-batch recovery. Back up and restore the replacement, rerun reconciliation and preserve the source snapshot. Rehearse delta extraction and a transaction freeze plan; explicitly avoid dual posting during cutover.'),
('6. Authorise cutover later', 'Functional owners validate reconciled workflows and reports on migrated data. Close critical gaps and security/performance/recovery defects. Only a later explicit user deployment instruction permits cutover. Keep a tested rollback window and a readable source archive. No deployment or production data transfer is part of this comparison.')]),
('End-to-end proof: commercial and buying', [
('J01 - Bid to released project', 'Import a BOQ with a bad unit and one building variant; quarantine the bad row, correct it, price assemblies and indirects, compare revisions, approve and hand over to quotation/project. Confirm exact quantities/rates, location mapping, original cost basis and independently released WBS budget. Builder today: not implemented.'),
('J02 - Demand to payment', 'Create unsourced multi-line demand; compare two vendors/currencies; approve reservation; split orders; partially receive and reject; return stock; match a bill and credit; allocate a partial payment and reconcile the bank. Prove no double cost, no orphan balances and preserved company/rate snapshots. Builder today: request portion only.'),
('J03 - Subcontract settlement', 'Award package; receive overclaimed application; accept part; return disputed work; certify retention/advance recovery; bill and partly pay; correct already billed work; approve amendment; reconcile final balance. Preserve every measured and financial stage. Builder today: examples only.'),
('J04 - Client measured certificate', 'Create cumulative quantities from previous approved certificate; add approved variation; technical return and new submission cycle; commercial then finance approval; produce draft invoice once; post separately; credit/correct and allocate receipt. Test simultaneous approvals and cumulative caps. Builder today: not implemented.'),
('J05 - Budget and forecast', 'Approve budget revision; incur stock/labour/service costs; clear accrual with bill; revise remaining work/risk; approve forecast; view item/floor/project/company reports at two cutoffs. Reconcile all totals, unallocated amounts, prior versions and findings. Builder today: seeded report only.'),
('J06 - Company and currency boundaries', 'Repeat buying with two companies sharing a supplier. Attempt cross-company project/PO/account references, unauthorised rate override and data export. Test intercompany resource charge with matching documents and group eliminations where required. Builder today: limited scope checks only.')]),
('End-to-end proof: site, people and closeout', [
('J07 - Quality to consequence', 'Use a superseded drawing in a proposed inspection, detect the revision problem, record failed concrete test/NCR, contain work, approve remedy, record waste/rework/time and independently verify closure. Reopen after failed retest. Check linked cost without duplication. Builder today: examples only.'),
('J08 - Change and delay', 'Log one instruction, notice deadline and affected activities; assess cost/time; revise price; record dispute and partial approval; amend budget/order/programme only through authorised steps. Build a source-backed timeline for EOT assessment. Builder today: examples only.'),
('J09 - Resources and people', 'Capture overnight attendance, leave correction, approved timesheet, crane custody transfer and maintenance downtime; import a repeated actuals batch. Confirm privacy, time balances, allocation, rates and one cost posting per source. Builder today: examples only.'),
('J10 - Partial handover', 'Accept one floor/system with tests, as-builts, O&M and client evidence; retain open snags elsewhere; start the appropriate defect obligation; reopen a defect; reconcile final account and release only eligible retention/security. Builder today: examples only.'),
('J11 - Reports and AI', 'Change filters/cutoff/permissions while paging and exporting every report family. Validate findings against full rows and source evidence. Inject a malicious instruction into a document; request a restricted company; simulate AI outage. Core workflows and deterministic reports must remain correct. Builder today: cost subset only; no AI integration.'),
('J12 - Migration and recovery', 'Import a complete snapshot twice, interrupt a batch, repair a quarantined row, restore backup and apply a delta. Reconcile counts, quantities, financial balances, attachment hashes and historical approvals. Demonstrate rollback with no duplicate postings. Builder today: no JAKH importer or rehearsal.')]),
('Delivery gates that prevent a repeat', [
('Gate A - Evidence and coverage', 'Before each domain build: every source destination is accounted for; core form fields, relationships, states, permissions, calculations, reports and exceptions have an evidence-backed contract. A menu-only row remains unresolved. The 267-row register is the starting accountability record, not a completed specification for all hidden behaviour.'),
('Gate B - Shared foundations', 'Implement typed company/project/work/location/party/catalogue models, production identity and policy authority, original accounting foundations, document/version storage and audit. Keep the current local data safe; evolve schema with tested migrations instead of deleting the database.'),
('Gate C - Connected operational increments', 'Build and validate bid/award/budget, procurement/stock/AP, subcontract measurement/settlement, client certification/AR and cost/forecast in their dependency order. Site/document/quality/programme/people/asset workflows connect to these same entities. Supporting and administrative functions retain explicit deliverables; sequencing is not scope removal.'),
('Gate D - Acceptance and examples', 'Each feature requires executable happy path, return/rejection, partial/correction, permission and reporting tests appropriate to its risks. Provide realistic examples demonstrating those operations, not static completion claims. Capture before/after evidence and map it back to the register IDs.'),
('Gate E - Migration and usability', 'Complete controlled import/reconciliation/recovery rehearsal; representative users complete the critical journeys with understandable labels and source-rich details. Verify keyboard, zoom, accessible errors, mobile field work and expected volumes. Any offline requirement needs an explicit conflict/queue model.'),
('Gate F - Local completion then deployment decision', 'No production readiness while critical gaps remain, and no deployment without the user later directing it. Keep meaningful work committed locally. GitHub remains the intended record, but pushes stay deferred. The source Git bundle contains code/docs, not the ignored SQLite runtime database.')]),
]

